  "body": "Found by the review of PR 1541 (non-blocking there).\n\nWhat happens: since PR 1541 the Passes tab shows Stepover only for the strategies that read it (Zigzag, Waterline, Auto). The stored value stays when the field is hidden. If that stored Stepover is zero or less, an Adaptive or Offset-rings operation is still refused, and the message names Stepover, a field the page no longer shows for that strategy, so the user cannot see what to fix.\n\nExpected: a strategy that never reads Stepover does not refuse on it; or the message says where the value is and how to change it.\n\nSafety note: this touches a parameter refusal of a toolpath generator. Zigzag, Waterline and Auto must keep refusing a stepover of zero or less and a stepover wider than the tool.\n\nDone means: an Adaptive and an Offset-rings operation with a stored Stepover of 0 generate as they do with a sane one (pinned by a test); Zigzag, Waterline and Auto still refuse it (pinned by a test).\n",
